ly uses it for personal relaxation.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It is an extension of her artistic vision and passion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'enigmatic' suggest about Eleanor?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"She is clearly identified and well-known.\",\n        \"Her personality is complex, but her work is straightforward.\",\n        \"She is a mysterious figure with hidden motives.\",\n        \"Her artwork has no depth or meaning.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"She is a mysterious figure with hidden motives.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the garden's impact on its patrons?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It only serves as a place for tourists to take pictures.\",\n        \"Patrons feel no connection with the garden's creator or its purpose.\",\n        \"They appreciate it as a unique space for relaxation and community engagement.\",\n        \"It is used solely by local wildlife, with no human interaction.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"They appreciate it as a unique space for relaxation and community engagement.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
